---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import { S } from '../data/sources.js';
const title = 'Opus Virtual Offices vs Davinci Virtual: Virtual Office Pricing Compared';
const description = 'Opus charges one flat price everywhere: $59/mo for an address or $99/mo with a live receptionist. Davinci prices each address separately ($50 to $200/mo in Houston, Miami and Los Angeles) plus a setup fee and a 6-month term. Side by side, with first-year costs. Checked Nov 23, 2026.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":"2026-11-23"};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-23" schema={schema}>
  <h1>Opus Virtual Offices vs Davinci Virtual</h1>
  <p class="lede">Both sell a business street address in an office building, with mail receipt and optional phone answering. The pricing models are opposite: Opus charges the same flat price at every location, while Davinci prices each building separately and adds a setup fee. Here's what each publishes, checked November 23, 2026.</p>

  <h2>Side by side</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Opus Virtual Offices</th><th>Davinci Virtual</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Address only</td><td>$59/mo, 100+ locations <Src href={S.opusBizAddr} /></td><td>Priced per location; "starting at $50" <Src href={S.davinciHome} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Address + live receptionist</td><td>$99/mo "all-inclusive," 650+ locations <Src href={S.opusBizAddr} /></td><td>Receptionist plans sold separately; the FAQ refers to Business and Premium plans and per-minute overage <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Setup fee</td><td>None: "no setup fee" on its Houston page <Src href={S.opusHouston} /></td><td>Address setup fee "starts at $150," includes an online notary; location listings show "+ Discounted setup fee" <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /> <Src href={S.davinciHouston} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Minimum term</td><td>3-month initial term, then month to month <Src href={S.opusHouston} /> <Src href={S.opusLa} label="LA" /></td><td>6-month commitment for location services, then month to month; 30 days' written notice to cancel <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mail</td><td>"Professional Mail Receipt" and "Digital Mail Notification"; staff sign for UPS, FedEx and DHL packages <Src href={S.opusHouston} /> <Src href={S.opusBizAddr} /></td><td>Mail and package receipt; forwarding on request, postage extra, "rates vary by location" <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mail forwarding fee</td><td>—</td><td>Varies by location <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Form 1583</td><td>Required: two IDs and a notary; online notarization accepted <Src href={S.opusBizAddr} /></td><td>Notarized form required before setup; online notary included in the setup fee <Src href={S.davinciFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Registered agent</td><td>$10/mo add-on, in the state of your office <Src href={S.opusServices} /></td><td>—</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Davinci address prices in three cities</h2>
  <p>Davinci's city pages list every building with its monthly address price. On November 23, 2026:</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>City</th><th>Davinci listings</th><th>Davinci address price</th><th>Opus address / all-inclusive</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Houston</td><td>57</td><td>$50 to $199/mo; 17 of the 57 at $50 <Src href={S.davinciHouston} /></td><td>$59 / $99 (3050 Post Oak Blvd) <Src href={S.opusHouston} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Miami</td><td>34</td><td>$50 to $200/mo <Src href={S.davinciMiami} /></td><td>$59 / $99 (848 Brickell Ave) <Src href={S.opusMiami} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>30</td><td>$50 to $185/mo <Src href={S.davinciLa} /></td><td>$59 / $99 (626 Wilshire Blvd) <Src href={S.opusLa} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="meta">Davinci prices exclude the setup fee and any receptionist plan <Src href={S.davinciFaq} />. Opus's New York (26 Broadway) page shows the same $59 and $99 prices <Src href={S.opusNy} />.</p>

  <h2>First-year cost, Houston</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Davinci, cheapest Houston address:</strong> $50 × 12 = $600, plus the setup fee (the FAQ says it starts at $150) <Src href={S.davinciHouston} /> <Src href={S.davinciFaq} />. That's $750 or more, with no phone answering.</li>
    <li><strong>Opus address only:</strong> $59 × 12 = $708, no setup fee <Src href={S.opusHouston} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Opus all-inclusive:</strong> $99 × 12 = $1,188, including a live receptionist on weekdays, a business phone and fax number, and voicemail and fax to email <Src href={S.opusServices} />.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you only need an address, the cheapest Davinci building and Opus come out close in year one, and Davinci gets cheaper from year two because the setup fee is one-time. If you want calls answered, Opus's flat $99 is simpler to price; Davinci quotes receptionist service separately <Src href={S.davinciFaq} />.</p>

  <h2>Opus add-ons</h2>
  <p>Opus lists these upgrades on its services page <Src href={S.opusServices} />: toll-free number, outbound calling app, texting, conference bridge, custom business email, registered agent and call recording at $10 a month each; extra extensions at $25 a month each; supervised transfer and message taking at $50 a month each. Receptionist hours are 8:30 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. weekdays (8 to 5 in the Pacific time zone) <Src href={S.opusServices} />.</p>

  <h2>Do you need a virtual office at all?</h2>
  <p>Both of these cost several times what a virtual mailbox does. If you need a street address and scanned mail but not a receptionist or a lobby listing, a virtual mailbox starts under $10 a month (see <a href="/virtual-office-vs-virtual-mailbox/">virtual office vs virtual mailbox</a> and <a href="/cheapest-virtual-mailbox-by-state/">the cheapest address by state</a>). Neither Opus nor Davinci publishes mail scanning prices on the pages we checked; if you want mail opened and scanned, see <a href="/virtual-mailbox-pricing-comparison/">virtual mailbox pricing compared</a>.</p>

  <h2>Links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><Aff id="opus" href="https://www.opusvirtualoffices.com/" text="Opus Virtual Offices" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="davinci" href="https://www.davincivirtual.com/" text="Davinci Virtual" /></li>
  </ul>
  <p>More: <a href="/virtual-mailbox-for-llc/">virtual mailbox for an LLC</a> · <a href="/virtual-mailbox-for-bank-account/">can I use a virtual address for a bank account?</a> · <a href="/">Mailbox Atlas home</a></p>
</Base>
